1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,670
A man is sitting in the dark, listening.

2
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:22,649
Imagine the cell with him. It is cut out of solid rock, and rock keeps every sound.
Water is dripping somewhere, slowly, always in the same place.

3
00:00:22,699 --> 00:00:34,854
When he shifts, the straw under him rustles, and the sound comes straight back off
the walls. The air is cool and still, and it smells of damp stone.

4
00:00:34,904 --> 00:00:47,149
From far above, through all that rock, comes something else. Music. Faint, like
something half remembered.

5
00:00:47,199 --> 00:00:51,410
There is a palace up there, and people in it who have had plenty to eat.

6
00:00:54,460 --> 00:01:05,906
Then footsteps in the passage outside. A guard, in no hurry. They come closer, pass
the door, and go on. He knows that walk by now.

7
00:01:05,956 --> 00:01:12,701
He was a man of the open air, who preached in the wilderness, beside a river, to
crowds.

8
00:01:12,751 --> 00:01:24,746
Now the world reaches him the way it reaches a blind man: by sound, and by what
other people tell him. So there is one sound he listens for above all the rest.

9
00:01:24,796 --> 00:01:39,683
A key in the lock. A bolt drawn back. A door so heavy that it groans. That sound
means a friend, let in for an hour, with news. And it is the news that troubles him.

10
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:50,528
He has been hearing things, secondhand, about a man he once pointed out to his own
followers. What he hears does not sound like what he expected.

11
00:01:50,578 --> 00:02:02,730
He cannot go and see for himself. So he sends two friends, on a walk of four days,
with one question. The answer he gets back ... begins with blind people.

12
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:20,550
This is Not By Sight, a series on blindness in the Bible, made by a blind Christian
for blind believers, their families, and the church.

13
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:29,880
The Scripture you will hear is the Berean Standard Bible, read word for word. The
thoughts marked as Brian's are Brian Clark's own.

14
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:34,124
And when we imagine a scene, we will tell you so.

15
00:02:34,174 --> 00:02:42,870
This is the last episode in our run through the healings in the Gospels, and it is
the one where Jesus Himself tells us what the healings were for.

16
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:54,953
First, where we are. John the Baptist baptised Jesus in the Jordan and pointed Him
out to his own followers.

17
00:02:55,003 --> 00:03:01,159
Then John rebuked Herod Antipas for taking his brother's wife, and Herod put him in
prison.

18
00:03:01,209 --> 00:03:10,007
Josephus, the Jewish historian, names the prison: Machaerus, a fortress east of the
Dead Sea, on the frontier.

19
00:03:10,057 --> 00:03:17,719
Edersheim describes it as a stronghold on sheer cliffs, built by one Jewish king and
enlarged by Herod the Great,

20
00:03:17,769 --> 00:03:21,950
with a palace at the top and dungeons cut into the rock below.

21
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,451
John the Baptist would die there. Where this is.

22
00:03:26,501 --> 00:03:34,132
Machaerus stands on the far side of the Dead Sea from everything else in this
series, and it is the farthest south we go.

23
00:03:34,182 --> 00:03:38,379
Stand on its walls and face north, with north at twelve o'clock.

24
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:47,191
Jericho is at eleven o'clock and Jerusalem at ten, and although both are close as
the crow flies, the Dead Sea lies in between,

25
00:03:47,241 --> 00:03:53,921
so a messenger had to walk round its northern end: about two days to Jerusalem by
way of Jericho.

26
00:03:53,971 --> 00:04:05,035
Straight ahead at twelve o'clock, up the whole length of the Jordan, is Galilee,
where Jesus was. Nazareth, Capernaum and Bethsaida are all about four days' walk.

27
00:04:05,085 --> 00:04:14,951
That is how far John's two friends had to go to ask one question, and how far they
had to come back with the answer. From that place he sends his question.

28
00:04:15,001 --> 00:04:20,370
Luke tells it with the most detail. Luke chapter 7, verses 18 to 23.

29
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:28,002
[Reader] Then John’s disciples informed him about all these things.

30
00:04:28,052 --> 00:04:38,595
[Reader] So John called two of his disciples and sent them to ask the Lord, “Are You
the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?”

31
00:04:38,645 --> 00:04:48,657
[Reader] When the men came to Jesus, they said, “John the Baptist sent us to ask,
‘Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?’”

32
00:04:48,707 --> 00:04:59,768
[Reader] At that very hour Jesus healed many people of their diseases, afflictions,
and evil spirits, and He gave sight to many who were blind.

33
00:04:59,818 --> 00:05:09,587
[Reader] So He replied, “Go back and report to John what you have seen and heard:
The blind receive sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear,

34
00:05:09,637 --> 00:05:13,656
[Reader] the dead are raised, and the good news is preached to the poor.

35
00:05:13,706 --> 00:05:16,690
[Reader] Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of Me.”

36
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:29,622
Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else? That is the
whole question. And it comes from the last man you would expect to ask it.

37
00:05:29,672 --> 00:05:41,278
Why would John, of all people, send it? Matthew Henry offers three possible reasons,
and they are worth taking one at a time. The first is the plainest.

38
00:05:41,328 --> 00:05:49,870
John wanted to be sure, for himself. He had given his whole life to announcing this
man, and a prisoner has a great deal of time to think.

39
00:05:55,920 --> 00:06:08,234
The second is harder to hear. John had been in that cell a long time. The One he had
announced was free, and healing strangers, and had not come for him.

40
00:06:08,284 --> 00:06:13,390
Henry suggests that the long imprisonment had made John wonder why Jesus did not
help him.

41
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:24,306
The third is the kindest to John. Perhaps he was not asking for himself at all. He
knew he might never leave that place.

42
00:06:24,356 --> 00:06:32,010
So he sent his followers to see Jesus with their own eyes, so that when he was gone,
they would know whom to follow.

43
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:47,643
We are not told which it was. And a person can ask one question for more than one
reason. Whatever the reason, Luke tells us what Jesus did before He answered a word.

44
00:06:47,693 --> 00:06:54,913
At that very hour He healed many, and gave sight to many who were blind.

45
00:06:54,963 --> 00:07:04,710
Henry takes the words literally: the messengers stayed perhaps an hour, and in that
hour saw enough. Then He told them what to say.

46
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:16,225
To hear the answer the way John heard it, you have to know what John knew. Jesus's
reply is built out of the prophet Isaiah.

47
00:07:16,275 --> 00:07:25,290
Here is the first passage, from a chapter about the day God Himself would come.
Isaiah chapter 35, verses 4 to 6.

48
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:42,254
[Reader] Say to those with anxious hearts: “Be strong, do not fear! Behold, your God
will come with vengeance. With divine retribution He will come to save you.”

49
00:07:42,304 --> 00:07:53,191
[Reader] Then the eyes of the blind will be opened and the ears of the deaf
unstopped. Then the lame will leap like a deer and the mute tongue will shout for
joy.

50
00:07:53,241 --> 00:07:57,650
[Reader] For waters will gush forth in the wilderness, and streams in the desert.

51
00:07:58,700 --> 00:08:07,130
And the second, the passage Jesus had already read aloud in the synagogue at
Nazareth. Isaiah chapter 61, verse 1.

52
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:15,855
[Reader] The Spirit of the Lord GOD is on Me, because the LORD has anointed Me to
preach good news to the poor.

53
00:08:15,905 --> 00:08:23,290
[Reader] He has sent Me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the
captives and freedom to the prisoners,

54
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:33,128
The eyes of the blind will be opened. Good news to the poor. Jesus did not say, I am
the one.

55
00:08:33,178 --> 00:08:41,626
He said, go and tell John what you see, and then He listed the things Isaiah had
said would happen when God came.

56
00:08:41,676 --> 00:08:46,667
John, who had Isaiah by heart, would have needed no explanation.

57
00:08:46,717 --> 00:08:54,593
Smith's dictionary says opening the eyes of the blind was understood as a peculiar
attribute of the promised one.

58
00:08:54,643 --> 00:08:58,930
Henry says the works spoke more plainly than any words could.

59
00:09:01,970 --> 00:09:08,613
Scripture gives us the question and the answer. It does not give us the messengers'
return.

60
00:09:08,663 --> 00:09:16,000
We imagine two tired men climbing back up to Machaerus with something to tell. This
is a scene, not Scripture.

61
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:30,560
[Disciple] Teacher. We are back. Yes, it is us, both of us. Sit, please, you should
sit.

62
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:33,440
[John] Well? Did you ask him? What did he say?

63
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:40,620
[Disciple] We asked him exactly as you said. Are you the one who was to come, or do
we wait for another?

64
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,190
[John] And his answer?

65
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:54,473
[Disciple] At first, nothing. He went on with what he was doing. There was a crowd,
as there always is, and people were being brought to him. We stood there an hour.

66
00:09:54,523 --> 00:10:02,370
[Disciple] A man who had been carried in walked out. A woman who was bent double
stood up straight. And there was a blind man.

67
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,990
[John] I see. ... Go on.

68
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:16,036
[Disciple] He was old, and someone had him by the arm, and Jesus touched his face,
and the man looked up, and he started to cry and to laugh at the same time,

69
00:10:16,086 --> 00:10:18,766
[Disciple] and he kept looking at his own hands.

70
00:10:18,816 --> 00:10:24,390
[Disciple] There were so many! More than one. So many. We lost count.

71
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,190
[John] The eyes of the blind will be opened.

72
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:36,905
[Disciple] Then he turned to us and said, go back and tell John what you have seen
and heard. The blind see. The lame walk.

73
00:10:36,955 --> 00:10:48,090
[Disciple] Lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, and the poor are
told the good news. And then he said one more thing, and I think it was for you.

74
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,390
[John] Say it.

75
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:52,810
[Disciple] Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of me.

76
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:07,150
John stayed in Machaerus. He was not healed, and he was not rescued. The answer he
got was wonders and signs for others.

77
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:21,872
And now, a word from Brian. Or rather, from the voice Brian picked for himself,
since he would not use his own. Around here we call it Mister Scaredy Cat.

78
00:11:21,922 --> 00:11:24,070
The voice is not his, but the words are.

79
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,470
[Brian] John the Baptist doubted.

80
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:36,117
[Brian] The man who pointed at Jesus and said, behold the Lamb of God, sat in a
dungeon and sent people to ask, are you the one, or should we wait for somebody
else.

81
00:11:36,167 --> 00:11:43,118
[Brian] For some reason, I find that enormously comforting. I think it means that
having doubt while in a dark place is not a failure of faith.

82
00:11:43,168 --> 00:11:53,382
[Brian] I think it is what faith sounds like when it is being tested, and it is
allowed to ask. Jesus did not answer with a sermon, or an argument, or a
proclamation.

83
00:11:53,432 --> 00:11:55,315
[Brian] He answered with people.

84
00:11:55,365 --> 00:12:05,591
[Brian] Luke says that at that very hour He healed many, and gave sight to many who
were blind, and then told John's messengers, go tell him what you have seen.

85
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:13,350
[Brian] When the question was, who are you, the answer began with blind people
seeing. I have heard that verse so many times and it still stops me.

86
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:25,246
Matthew tells the same exchange more briefly, and we will hear it, for two reasons.
Matthew says John heard in prison about the works of Christ.

87
00:12:25,296 --> 00:12:36,051
It was the works that reached him, through the walls. And Matthew goes straight on
to what Jesus said next, once John's friends had started for home.

88
00:12:36,101 --> 00:12:38,890
Matthew chapter 11, verses 2 to 11.

89
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:50,547
[Reader] Meanwhile John heard in prison about the works of Christ, and he sent his
disciples to ask Him, “Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for
someone else?”

90
00:12:50,597 --> 00:13:04,235
[Reader] Jesus replied, “Go back and report to John what you hear and see: The blind
receive sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are
raised,

91
00:13:04,285 --> 00:13:07,699
[Reader] and the good news is preached to the poor.

92
00:13:07,749 --> 00:13:12,033
[Reader] Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of Me.”

93
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:23,092
[Reader] As John’s disciples were leaving, Jesus began to speak to the crowds about
John: “What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed swaying in the wind?

94
00:13:23,142 --> 00:13:36,181
[Reader] Otherwise, what did you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? Look,
those who wear fine clothing are found in kings’ palaces. What then did you go out
to see?

95
00:13:36,231 --> 00:13:41,152
[Reader] A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.

96
00:13:41,202 --> 00:13:50,100
[Reader] This is the one about whom it is written: ‘Behold, I will send My messenger
ahead of You, who will prepare Your way before You.’

97
00:13:50,150 --> 00:14:00,930
[Reader] Truly I tell you, among those born of women there has risen no one greater
than John the Baptist. Yet even the least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than
he.

98
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:06,925
Did you hear when He said it? As John's disciples were leaving.

99
00:14:06,975 --> 00:14:16,973
Jesus waited until they were on the road, and then He turned to the crowd and spoke
about the man in the cell. Not a reed swaying in the wind.

100
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:30,470
Not a man in fine clothes. Those, He says, are found in kings' palaces. John was
underneath one. A prophet, and more than a prophet.

101
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:42,787
Among those born of women there has risen no one greater. So the doubt did not lower
John in His eyes. The question was allowed. It was answered.

102
00:14:42,837 --> 00:14:50,670
And the man who asked it was given the highest praise Jesus ever gave anyone, in the
same hour.

103
00:14:56,555 --> 00:15:02,014
[Brian] I have to be honest about the other side of it. I am a blind believer, and
my eyes have not been opened.

104
00:15:02,064 --> 00:15:12,726
[Brian] The healings in these episodes were signs, and signs point to something.
They pointed John to who Jesus was. They point me there too, without my sight coming
back.

105
00:15:12,776 --> 00:15:19,145
[Brian] I would be lying if I said I never asked for it. I would also be lying if I
said that is what this verse is about.

106
00:15:19,195 --> 00:15:27,285
[Brian] This verse is not a promise that every blind person who believes will be
healed in this life. It is Jesus answering a question about Himself.

107
00:15:27,335 --> 00:15:36,907
[Brian] John asked, are You the One. And Jesus said, look at what is happening
around Me, and remember what Isaiah said would happen when God came.

108
00:15:36,957 --> 00:15:44,771
[Brian] The healings were the proof of who He is. That proof still stands, whether
or not my own eyes are ever opened on this side of heaven.

109
00:15:44,821 --> 00:15:52,313
[Brian] I do not need my sight back to know who He is. I know who He is. Blessed is
the one who does not fall away on account of Me.

110
00:15:52,363 --> 00:16:00,777
[Brian] That is the last line of the answer, and I think it was aimed at John, in
prison, who was not going to be healed or rescued and knew it.

111
00:16:00,827 --> 00:16:07,027
[Brian] Jesus was telling him: do not let what I am not doing for you make you doubt
what I am.

112
00:16:07,077 --> 00:16:12,530
[Brian] Every blind believer who has prayed for sight and gotten up the next morning
still blind has heard that line.

113
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:28,757
Look back over the six episodes. A man born blind sent to wash. Bartimaeus shouting
by the road. A man at Bethsaida who saw trees walking and said so.

114
00:16:28,807 --> 00:16:38,930
Two men who followed by sound into a house, and one who could not speak for himself.
Crowds on a mountain and in the Temple.

115
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:51,025
And now this: when the greatest prophet asked who Jesus was, Jesus pointed at all of
them. The blind receive sight.

116
00:16:51,075 --> 00:17:02,770
Not because blindness was the worst thing, and not because sight was the point, but
because Isaiah had said that when God came, this is what it would look like.

117
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:07,790
Blind people were not left at the edges. They were at the top of the list.

118
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:17,461
[Brian] The part of this episode that comes closest to home for me is not about eyes
at all. It is in the verse from Isaiah that Jesus read at Nazareth.

119
00:17:17,511 --> 00:17:25,736
[Brian] He has sent Me to bind up the brokenhearted. The work that everyone in our
house does puts us straight in the path of the brokenhearted.

120
00:17:25,786 --> 00:17:35,371
[Brian] It is less a job than a way of life, and it is far harder than most people
can imagine. But I am grateful for what it has done to my heart. It keeps me humble.

121
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:43,873
[Brian] It teaches me to honor other people the way God wants us to, because every
one of us is made in His image. I know that someday I will see again.

122
00:17:43,923 --> 00:17:53,318
[Brian] I have always known it, because I was blessed to have parents who led me to
the Lord when I was very young. They say blindness is the second greatest fear
people have.

123
00:17:53,368 --> 00:18:02,141
[Brian] I take no comfort in that. But I can tell you, from inside it, that
blindness is not something to fear at all. What scares me is something else.

124
00:18:02,191 --> 00:18:06,958
[Brian] It is the people who have to carry this burden without knowing the grace and
mercy of our Savior,

125
00:18:07,008 --> 00:18:11,130
[Brian] and without knowing the great joys that lie ahead for those of us who belong
to Him.

126
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:29,564
This has been Not By Sight. The full story, with every source named, is at
blindnessinthebible.com.

127
00:18:29,614 --> 00:18:40,500
Scripture quotations are from the Holy Bible, Berean Standard Bible, which is in the
public domain. The scenes you heard marked as imagined are our own.

128
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:47,810
Everything else is from the text and the old books. For we walk by faith, not by
sight.

